# The modem's bytes arrive while the kernel writes its log on COM2, which
# shares IRQ3 with the modem's COM4. Bochs drops COM4's interrupt when COM2
# is touched; the timer fetches what a lost interrupt leaves, so the answer
# still comes whole (30 bytes: ATI and CR echoed, the name, OK).
program: devices
define: DEVICES_SHARED_IRQ
modem: hayes
match: contains
timeout: 60
emulators: bochs dosbox-x
---
modem: idle: answer of 30 bytes
modem: while the log is written: answer of 30 bytes
modem: after: answer of 30 bytes
